# Workflow scripts must stay LF-only. Git's autocrlf rewrites them to CRLF on checkout, and the Workflow tool's
# permission layer refuses a script containing control characters — CR is one — so a CRLF'd script cannot be
# launched at all. The failure message ("script contains control characters") does not name the cause.
.claude/workflows/*.js text eol=lf

# DEVLOG.md is the ONE tracked file stored with CRLF in the object database (every other text file normalizes to
# LF under core.autocrlf). That was implicit — no attribute governed it — and the log's append discipline depends
# on it: entries are inserted by writing BYTES, and a silent renormalization would rewrite all 36k lines in a
# single diff. Declaring it here makes the exception intentional and immune to `git add --renormalize`.
# This matches what Git already does, so it introduces no diff.
DEVLOG.md -text
